### Manual tests for Creator Tracker API
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request"), or copy into curl.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. List creators -> 200
GET {{base}}/api/creators

### 2. Valid creator -> 201
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "MrBeast", "platform": "YouTube", "followers": 250000000 }

### 3. Blank name -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "   ", "platform": "Instagram", "followers": 100 }

### 4. followers = 0 -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zero", "platform": "Instagram", "followers": 0 }

### 5. followers = -5 -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Negative", "platform": "Instagram", "followers": -5 }

### 6. followers = 12.5 -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Decimal", "platform": "Instagram", "followers": 12.5 }

### 7. followers = "abc" -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Text", "platform": "Instagram", "followers": "abc" }

### 8. Bad platform -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "TikToker", "platform": "TikTok", "followers": 100 }

### 9. Broken JSON -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/creators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Broken", "platform": "YouTube",
